---
import Article from '../layouts/Article.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Article
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="SalaryLens privacy policy — we do not collect or store your salary data. All calculations run in your browser."
  path="/privacy/"
  updated="Aug 2026"
  showCta={false}
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is built to be private by default. This policy explains what we do and don't collect.
  </p>

  <h2>Salary data stays in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Every calculation on this site runs entirely in your browser (client-side). The CTC and other
    numbers you enter are <strong>never sent to us or any server</strong>, and we do not store them.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics to count page views and understand which pages are
    useful. This does not identify you and does not track you across other sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Email (optional)</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose to subscribe to updates, we store only the email address you provide, solely to
    send occasional salary and tax tips. You can unsubscribe at any time via the link in any email.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Outbound links (for example to the Chrome Web Store) are governed by those sites' own privacy
    policies. We don't sell or share your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Reach out via the {SITE.name} Chrome Web Store listing or GitHub.</p>
</Article>
